<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch-integers" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Integers</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      Integers extend the natural numbers by including zero and negative numbers: <m>\ldots, -3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, \ldots</m>
    </p>
    <p>
      They allow us to represent quantities below zero — temperatures, debts, sea levels — and perform operations in both directions on the number line.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="num_integers-intro.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="num_integers-operations.ptx" />

</chapter>
